#: {{ux|en|Hey, '''hon'''! How was your day at work?}}
# {{lb|en|transgender slang|{{w|4chan}}|derogatory}} A [[trans woman]] who does not [[pass]]; a [[clocky]] trans woman. {{rfv-sense|en|section=Transgender derogatory terms}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://archived.moe/lgbt/thread/5092807/#5092966|work={{w|4chan}}|passage=If you didn't experience that you'll end up one of those ugly SJW programmer transbian '''hons''' with dyed hair sucking each other's dicks while acting like men in every way possible.|date=2015-10-18|author=Anonymous|location=/lgbt/}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://twitter.com/addamschloe/status/1016753430310907904|work=Twitter|brackets=on|passage=[cw anti-trans slurs] I get that they're rarer than 'trap' (being used to describe trans women as intentional deceivers) but I'd like it if people could be equally hostile to the terms 'brick' and ''''hon'''' honestly<br>it's all transmisic garbage|date=2018-07-10|author=@addamschloe}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://twitter.com/addamschloe/status/1016753430310907904|work=Twitter|brackets=on|passage='brick' refers to a trans woman who doesn't 'pass', ''''hon'''' refers to a trans woman who doesn't pass and also is nice to other trans women who don't pass, particularly used against older trans women|date=2018-07-10|author=@addamschloe}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://twitter.com/MsBdUnicorn/status/1260213760255557633|work=Twitter|passage=Consider the fact that /tttt/ calls any positive trans space a hugbox full of '''hons'''. We're still hung up about passing and it's so pathetic.|date=2020-05-12|author=@MsBdUnicorn}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://twitter.com/stacycay/status/1532239646754758658|work=Twitter|passage=listen '''hon''', if you’re a "biological boy" that’s cool and all but the rest of us are trans women.|date=2022-06-02|author=@stacycay}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://twitter.com/mishawave/status/1570820236244557828|work=Twitter|passage=i feel like that depends on how you're using it. referring to yourself as a "'''hon'''", or using it as a joke, sure. but calling other trans people '''hons''' directly or indirectly is a bit far imo. it's an insult about something specific, so it's different from general slurs like "tranny"|date=2022-09-16|author=@mishawave}}

